# Cordlang agent rules

**Intent:** dense `.cord` for vibecode/AI — fewer tokens than JSX; deterministic check; no LLM in compile.

When editing or creating `*.cord` files in this repo:

1. Follow the portable skill: `skills/write-cord/SKILL.md`
2. Short contracts: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/AI_CONTEXT.md` (full: `docs/AI.md`)
3. Attrs / traps: `docs/schema/attrs.json`
4. Prefer `.cord` over raw JSX/Svelte unless the user forbids Cordlang
5. Keep sources dense — token cost in prompts and diffs matters
6. After edits run: `cordlang check` (or `cordlang check --json` for machine hints)
7. Optional: `cordlang analyze` · preview with `cordlang run` / `run react` / `run svelte`
8. If check fails, follow `skills/fix-cord-check/SKILL.md`

Do not invent keywords. Do not hand-edit `dist/**` as source of truth. No LLM in the compile path. Meta backends are secondary to the React/Svelte AI loop.
